---
const faqs = [
  {
    number: '01',
    question: 'How long does a project take, and what do you actually need from my side to start?',
    paragraphs: [
      'Most business owners in India do not have the time to write lengthy technical briefs or 20-page requirement documents. You do not need to prepare any technical files. A 20-minute phone call, a quick WhatsApp chat, or forwarding a few photos of your business, menu, resort, or service list is more than enough to get us started. We handle the copywriting, structure, design, and technical setup for you.',
      'For websites, launch timelines are strictly 7 to 14 days. We do not drag projects out for months. Within 3 to 4 days of kickoff, you receive a private staging link on your phone to review the real, responsive design. For custom dashboards or business automations (like spreadsheet sync or automated WhatsApp/PDF pipelines), sprints typically take 2 to 3 weeks with defined weekly milestones where you test the working build directly.',
      'Once you review and approve the final version, we connect your custom domain (.com, .in, etc.) and deploy the site live to global edge servers in under an hour. You also receive full administrative access and simple 2-minute video walkthroughs so your team can manage inquiries easily.'
    ]
  },
  {
    number: '02',
    question: 'How does pricing and payment work? Are there any hidden charges or surprise monthly fees?',
    paragraphs: [
      'We work on a straightforward fixed-scope model with zero surprise invoices. For starter and business websites, payment is split into two simple milestones: 50% upfront to initiate design and development, and the remaining 50% only after the project is fully completed, tested, and approved by you. For larger web applications, we use a 50/30/20 milestone structure tied directly to live working demos.',
      'Traditional agencies in India often charge hidden fees for "SSL certificates", "server setup fees", or "mandatory annual maintenance". We do not do that. We host static websites on Cloudflare\'s global edge network, which is free, lightning-fast, and includes free SSL encryption. Your only recurring external cost is your domain registration (typically ₹800 to ₹1,200 per year on Cloudflare or Namecheap), which remains 100% in your own name and under your direct account.',
      'Once your site is live, it belongs entirely to you. You are never locked into monthly subscriptions or forced maintenance contracts. If you ever need updates down the road, you can request them on a simple pay-as-you-go basis (from ₹1,000 for minor updates) or opt for a lightweight support retainer only if your business needs active weekly changes.'
    ]
  },
  {
    number: '03',
    question: 'Who will actually be working on my project, and how do we communicate during work?',
    paragraphs: [
      'You collaborate 1-on-1 directly with Shiva Sajay. In conventional software agencies, senior executives close the sale and immediately pass your work to inexperienced junior interns or third-party freelancers. At Nira Studio, the person who discusses your business needs is the same engineer writing your code, configuring your database, and testing your forms.',
      'We communicate through direct channels that small business owners actually use every day—mainly WhatsApp messages, direct phone calls, and short Loom screen-recording videos. You don\'t have to log into confusing Jira ticketing boards, Slack workspaces, or sit through unnecessary one-hour Zoom meetings just to ask a quick question.',
      'Because there are no account managers or middlemen in between, decisions that usually take days at an agency happen in minutes. If you want a headline changed, an image swapped, or an inquiry button updated, you send a quick WhatsApp note and it gets done directly.'
    ]
  },
  {
    number: '04',
    question: 'Will this actually bring real customer inquiries, and how does WhatsApp integration work?',
    paragraphs: [
      'In India, over 85% of your customers visit your website from a smartphone, usually on mobile 4G or 5G connections. If a website takes 5 seconds to load or asks visitors to fill out a long, clunky form, they leave and call your competitor. Every website we build is engineered to load in under 1 second on mobile devices, with crisp typography and zero heavy theme bloat.',
      'Instead of forcing customers to type into formal email contact forms, we build high-converting 1-tap WhatsApp buttons throughout the website. When an interested customer taps "Inquire on WhatsApp", it immediately launches WhatsApp on their phone with a pre-filled message specifying the exact room, service, or product they were viewing. This lets you reply instantly while their buying intent is highest.',
      'If your business deals with repetitive manual processes—such as dispatching hundreds of invoices, sending booking confirmations, or generating monthly employee payslips—we can automate the entire pipeline using WhatsApp Cloud API and email workers, completely eliminating spreadsheet copy-paste errors.'
    ]
  }
];
---

<section class="py-12 sm:py-20 lg:py-32 bg-[#F5F2EB]" id="faq">
  <div class="max-w-4xl mx-auto px-4 sm:px-6 lg:px-8">
    
    <!-- Clean Minimal Header -->
    <div class="mb-6 sm:mb-12" data-reveal data-y="16">
      <h2 class="font-display font-extrabold text-3xl sm:text-5xl text-[#0D111C] tracking-tight leading-tight">
        FAQs
      </h2>
    </div>

    <!-- Editorial Underlined Accordion List -->
    <div class="border-t border-[#D1CABE]" id="faq-accordion-group" data-reveal-group>
      {faqs.map((faq, index) => (
        <div
          class="faq-item border-b border-[#D1CABE] transition-colors duration-200"
          data-open="false"
          data-index={index}
          data-reveal-item
        >
          <button
            type="button"
            class="faq-trigger w-full py-4 sm:py-7 lg:py-8 flex items-center justify-between gap-4 sm:gap-6 text-left cursor-pointer focus:outline-none select-none group"
            aria-expanded="false"
          >
            <div class="flex items-baseline gap-3 sm:gap-6 pointer-events-none">
              <span class="font-mono text-xs sm:text-sm font-bold text-[#0B3C85]/60 flex-shrink-0">
                {faq.number}
              </span>
              <span class="font-display font-bold text-base sm:text-xl lg:text-2xl text-[#0D111C] group-hover:text-[#0B3C85] transition-colors duration-200 leading-snug">
                {faq.question}
              </span>
            </div>

            <!-- Top-Right Inclined Arrow (↗) - Raw outside of any circle -->
            <span class="faq-arrow-wrapper text-[#0B3C85] group-hover:text-[#0D111C] flex items-center justify-center flex-shrink-0 transition-colors pointer-events-none p-1">
              <svg
                xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg"
                width="18"
                height="18"
                viewBox="0 0 24 24"
                fill="none"
                stroke="currentColor"
                stroke-width="2"
                stroke-linecap="round"
                stroke-linejoin="round"
                class="faq-arrow-icon transition-transform duration-300 ease-[cubic-bezier(0.16,1,0.3,1)]"
              >
                <line x1="7" y1="17" x2="17" y2="7"></line>
                <polyline points="7 7 17 7 17 17"></polyline>
              </svg>
            </span>
          </button>
          
          <!-- Butter-smooth Accordion Content Container -->
          <div class="faq-content overflow-hidden max-h-0 opacity-0 transition-all duration-400 ease-[cubic-bezier(0.16,1,0.3,1)]">
            <div class="pl-6 sm:pl-10 pr-2 sm:pr-4 pb-5 sm:pb-8 pt-1 text-sm sm:text-base text-neutral-600 font-body leading-relaxed max-w-3xl space-y-3 sm:space-y-4">
              {faq.paragraphs.map((p) => (
                <p>{p}</p>
              ))}
            </div>
          </div>
        </div>
      ))}
    </div>

  </div>
</section>

<script>
  function initFaqAccordion() {
    const group = document.getElementById('faq-accordion-group');
    if (!group) return;

    if (group.dataset.initialized === 'true') return;
    group.dataset.initialized = 'true';

    const items = group.querySelectorAll<HTMLElement>('.faq-item');

    function closeItem(item: HTMLElement) {
      item.setAttribute('data-open', 'false');
      const trigger = item.querySelector<HTMLButtonElement>('.faq-trigger');
      const content = item.querySelector<HTMLElement>('.faq-content');
      const arrow = item.querySelector<HTMLElement>('.faq-arrow-icon');

      if (trigger) trigger.setAttribute('aria-expanded', 'false');
      if (content) {
        content.style.maxHeight = '0px';
        content.style.opacity = '0';
      }
      if (arrow) {
        arrow.style.transform = 'rotate(0deg)';
      }
    }

    function openItem(item: HTMLElement) {
      item.setAttribute('data-open', 'true');
      const trigger = item.querySelector<HTMLButtonElement>('.faq-trigger');
      const content = item.querySelector<HTMLElement>('.faq-content');
      const arrow = item.querySelector<HTMLElement>('.faq-arrow-icon');

      if (trigger) trigger.setAttribute('aria-expanded', 'true');
      if (content) {
        content.style.maxHeight = `${content.scrollHeight + 32}px`;
        content.style.opacity = '1';
      }
      if (arrow) {
        arrow.style.transform = 'rotate(90deg)';
      }
    }

    items.forEach((item) => {
      const trigger = item.querySelector<HTMLButtonElement>('.faq-trigger');
      if (!trigger) return;

      trigger.addEventListener('click', (e) => {
        e.preventDefault();
        const isOpen = item.getAttribute('data-open') === 'true';

        items.forEach((other) => {
          if (other !== item) {
            closeItem(other);
          }
        });

        if (isOpen) {
          closeItem(item);
        } else {
          openItem(item);
        }
      });
    });
  }

  initFaqAccordion();
  document.addEventListener('astro:page-load', initFaqAccordion);
</script>
